otal":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nStarted happening in 4.5\n\n### System information\n\nWin 10, Linux, Godot 4.5\n\n### Issue description\n\nLinux (super super random and not easily reproducible) \nWin 10   \n\nThe issue seems to be with the focus switching back after having run the game in windowed mode. \non linux, i saw it randomly maybe one or two times, the win10 folk seem to have it happen more often though. \n\nafter closing the game window, the focus is now not in 2D or Scripts or wherever one was before, but in the game tab, with the wrong message showing:\ninstead of \"Embedding is disabled\" it says \"Press play to start the game\" \n\nI'm assuming it has to do with new a11y features, but somewhere the original start point gets lost, so it defaults the focus back to the game tab (?)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI'm on Linux and can't easily reproduce it but on win 10 it seems easily reproducible ( can't test myself but here's what people in the discord did) \n\n\"This may also be a side effect of accidentally resizing the window before closing it.\nYep! 100% repro if I accidentally glance the window's resize border before clicking close. [...]\n\n- click Play\n- game window opens but editor is still on 2D mode, showing my scene\n- play game, editor, in the background, remains on 2D mode \n- interact with any options on the Game bar. Editor, in the background remains in 2D mode, showing the scene I was on\n- close game window: editor suddenly switches to Game mode and shows the message (but only if I interacted with the Game window or icons in any way) \" \n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nnot dependent on specific project","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.